{% lede %}
At Autodesk I made the videos that explained Ember, an open-source stereolithography 3D printer: who was using it, what its features did, and how to keep it running. The Glidewell video, about Ember's largest customer printing dental crowns and copings, has 168,000 views.
{% /lede %}

I wrote, directed, filmed, illustrated and edited the videos. Customer stories like Glidewell and Origin Laboratories showed the printer in production. Feature videos like VariSlice, sub-pixel printing and Pattern Mode used animation to show ideas a camera can't see, like how a projector's pixels build a layer.

## Print process

Alongside the videos I researched how the printer works: which design features are hard to print with stereolithography, and the steepest overhang that prints accurately without supports. Work I contributed to on improving vertical walls was issued a U.S. patent, *Enhanced Three Dimensional Printing of Vertical Edges* (US 10,780,641 B2).

Click any thumbnail to watch. View counts as of April 2026.
